@Xichen96 - reviewed exact head `1a266d83e680f684d30a13abc872318305975f70`. The previously noted oversized-required-VRF path is now fixed: it returns failure and `from_client()` drops the request instead of forwarding without VSS.

The current implementation looks ready from a code-review perspective. The VSS-required fail-closed policy is narrowly applied, ordinary non-VSS RFC 3046 fallback is preserved, the projected size includes the two-byte Option 82 header, and DCO/CLA/security plus amd64, arm64, and armhf CI are all green.

Non-blocking follow-ups: add overflow-policy coverage for `append`/`replace` relay modes and assert the TX drop-counter increments. The PR description also references an older published head/build and could be refreshed to the current exact head.

@StormLiangMS Thanks. The oversized-required-VRF path now returns failure and has focused drop coverage in `e4e694f`.

On forward mode, I initially made the same assumption and opened sonic-buildimage#29111. @ashutosh-agrawal explained that the request class must be identified first: `giaddr == 0` is a first-hop request owned by this relay and receives local VSS, while `giaddr != 0` is already relayed and forward mode preserves the client-facing relay's `giaddr` and Option 82. I agreed, so #29111 is closed.

That correction required a substantial new revision of #122: it now establishes reply ownership before VSS handling and preserves already-relayed forward-mode traffic. The generic ownership portion has been split into #147.

@vaibhavhd, could you please approve the requested 202605 backport?

Additional exact validation of sonic-mgmt `test_dhcp_relay_with_source_port_ip_in_relay_enabled` covered all four affected dual-ToR hardware families: Arista-7260CX3-D108C8, Arista-7260CX3-C64, Arista-7050CX3-32C-C32, and Cisco-8101C01-C32. With the corresponding sonic-mgmt fixes, ISC passes end-to-end on every family, while SONiC alone still fails at relayed Discover with `0 != 48`.

Packet capture confirms the current 202605 relay emits Link Selection `192.168.0.0`; the corrected expectation and this PR use the receiving VLAN address `192.168.0.1`. The 202605 buildimage pin is still `dae12809`, before this fix. This backport is required for sonic-mgmt #26108 and the exact source-port-IP testcase to pass on 202605; an xfail would hide the product defect.
